Closed by `3658f32` (`spec: destroy every PIN-digest copy off the node hosts before funding, and name SEC-10's digest premise wherever silence is scoped (bps-363)`), on top of the claim `5da4f50`; base `6f6c537`. Every check below was run on the landed tree after its last edit, with no other build running on it.

**The acceptance criteria**

- **Edits 1 and 2.** `OPS-35`'s and `OPS-24`'s whole paragraphs equal the Agent Brief's block quotes with their `> ` markers removed (whitespace-normalized).
- **Edit 3.** `MAN-32`'s sentence is the Agent Brief's. The replaced sentence occurs nowhere else.
- **Edits 4 to 11.** Each new text occurs exactly once in its file, whitespace-normalized, and each replaced text occurs nowhere outside its new text. Edit 11 is four bullets, the second in both `Silence.lean` and `Alerts.lean`. Edits 8, 11.1 and 11.4 sit directly after their anchors, in the anchor's paragraph.
  - Each file was also rebuilt as its base text plus the edits, cut from this bead's last comment, and compared with the tree: all 11 files are equal, with the same paragraph count; `ADR-0021` has three more paragraphs, the new section.
  - Five phrases of the description's superseded wording occur nowhere in the set.
- **Edit 12.** `ADR-0021` ends with `## Decision 2026-10-21: PIN-digest copies`, after the 2026-10-05 section, word for word. `git diff 6f6c537 -- docs/adr/0012-model-b-spend-and-duress-architecture.md` prints nothing.
- **Quotes the citation gate does not check** (under four words, or attributed to an ADR), checked by grep: "release-history premise" and "digest premise" occur in `SEC-10`'s body; "Silence model A" and "who has compromised **no node**" occur once each in `ADR-0012`. No quotation of any replaced text is left stale anywhere in the set.
- **Full gate.** `nix develop --command bash tools/check-all.sh`, unpiped and redirected to a file, exits 0; all nine gates PASS.
- **Citation gate as a script.** Exit 0: "quoted attributions verified: 880, 522 of them in Lean docstrings: clean", "unquoted attributions: 0: clean", the base's figures. The per-file count of verified quoted attributions is unchanged in every file: none fell, none rose.
- **Scope.** `git diff 6f6c537 --stat` touches exactly the 11 files the twelve edits name, plus `.beads/issues.jsonl`.
  - Under `tools/` and `.github/` only the two module docstrings differ; everything outside each docstring is byte-identical. No baseline file changed.
  - The paragraphs holding the four opening sentences (`README.md` "a silent duress response", `00-overview.md` "looks identical to the normal one and silently arms a sweep of the whole vault", `CONTEXT.md` "silently sweeps the vault to an independent escape wallet", `executive-summary.md` "silently arms the Escape") are byte-identical to the base.
  - So are `SEC-2` A4, `SEC-54` rows 9, 11 and 16, `OPS-25` and `OPS-63`. "but no node" still stands in `DUR-1` and `OVR-13`.
  - Every anchor `bps-xyu`'s brief quotes from this bead's new wording occurs exactly once.
- **Review.** Four reviewers read the change in their own clones. None found a defect; three report a green full gate there. Two suggested rewrapping three paragraph tails the edits had left ragged (`DOM-2`, and one each in the two module docstrings). They were rewrapped before the commit, whitespace only.

**Criterion 5: the other statements of the silence scope**

Swept for `silen`, `SILENCE`, `release-history premise`, `scope of SILENCE`, `no node`, `PIN digest`, `identical` and `indistinguishable` across the numbered documents, `docs/adr/`, `CONTEXT.md`, `executive-summary.md`, `README.md` and the Lean docstrings, each hit read in its paragraph.

What changed: the twelve edits, and nothing else. No statement outside them claims silence against a holder of a digest copy, or gives its premises or exclusions as complete while leaving the digest premise out.

Checked and unchanged:

- **Agree once the edits are in**, naming no complete premise list that omits the digest premise:
  - `SEC-10`'s opening scope sentence and `SEC-26`;
  - `SEC-47`, `DUR-36`, `OPS-54`, `OPR-21`;
  - `OPR-66`'s "restoration of SILENCE" and `CNF-122`;
  - `CONTEXT.md`'s **Concealment horizon**;
  - `F60`;
  - the coupling, horizon and theorem docstrings of `BtcPolicy.Silence`.
- **Carry the scope by citing its owner** (`DUR-1`, `SEC-10`):
  - `SEC-8`, `OVR-5`, `SEC-2` A5;
  - `CONTEXT.md`'s "silence" usage rule ("always scoped (`SEC-10`)"), **Pin-independent ingress** and **Observer projection**;
  - the executive summary's "Subject to the scope below";
  - `API-20`, `API-21`, `API-25`, `SPN-41`, `DUR-5`, `DUR-10`;
  - `DEF-11`, `F22`, `CNF-40` to `CNF-44`, `CNF-55`, `CNF-140`, `CNF-152`;
  - `07-node-api.md`'s "`DUR-1`'s SILENCE compares one node's bytes";
  - the `Pin` and `obsPair` docstrings ("the adversary `SEC-10` names");
  - `ADR-0023` decision 14.
- **State no scope**, which is `bps-axj`'s audit, the class the owner put the four opening sentences in:
  - the four opening sentences;
  - `CONTEXT.md`'s **Duress PIN** ("Externally identical to the normal PIN.");
  - `05`'s opening paragraph and `DUR-1`'s first sentences;
  - `SPN-3`, `SEC-20`, `SEC-25`, `SEC-53`, `OPS-68`;
  - `ADR-0008`, `ADR-0014`'s pin-uniform budget argument and `ADR-0017`'s end-to-end evidence;
  - `README.md`'s later silence mentions.
- **Owned by another bead or recorded in an ADR decision:**
  - `SEC-2` A4 and `SEC-54` row 9 (`bps-amt` adds the digest premise to both cells);
  - row 11 (`bps-xyu`) and row 16 (`bps-amt`; its silence sentence concerns the release-history premise and claims nothing against a digest holder);
  - "but no node" (`bps-xyu`);
  - `OPS-25` and `OPS-63` (`bps-ay1`);
  - `ADR-0012`'s "Silence model A" and its accepted residuals, narrowed by edit 12 and not edited;
  - `ADR-0021`'s decision of 2026-10-05;
  - `ADR-0026`, `ADR-0027` and `ADR-0028`; `ADR-0028`'s quotation of `DUR-1` still occurs in it;
  - the `F66` row.

**Counterexample reading.** No requirement this bead leaves alone keeps, backs up, restores or re-derives from a node configuration, the ceremony input or `ceremony-state.json` after funding. Read: `MAN-20`, `MAN-24`, `MAN-27`, `MAN-29` to `MAN-34`, `MAN-36`, `MAN-40`, `OPR-10`, `OPR-78`, `OPR-80`, `WIR-14`, `OPS-1`, `OPS-9`, `OPS-21`, `OPS-25`, `OPS-30`, `OPS-36`, `OPS-53`, `OPS-61` to `OPS-63`, `STO-1`, `SEC-1`, `SEC-21` to `SEC-23`, `SEC-28`, `DOM-3`, `DOM-4`, `DOM-10`, `CNF-114`.

- `SEC-21`'s "It cannot redirect funds, cause arbitrary bytes to be broadcast, create a new attacker-authorized spend, or steal." and `DOM-3` are written for `DOM-2`'s coordinator, whose boundary edit 7 makes depend on the digest premise.
- `OPR-78`'s confirmation and `MAN-40`'s flag are kept in the audit-records file edit 1 requires.
- `OPS-30`'s successor-PIN recommendation needs neither the old digests nor "predecessor-digest persistence".

**Follow-up, for `bps-ay1`.** `OPS-24` now says the node configurations "are not part of" the backup set, and `OPS-35` says "No copy is kept as a backup". `OPS-63`'s "(2) restore from backup onto a fresh machine" still asks for a node restore. A reviewer noted that the former `OPS-24`, "The sealed backup set (`MAN-33`) MUST be moved off the coordinator", could be read as including the node configurations. So `bps-ay1` should cite the new `OPS-24` and `OPS-35` rather than argue that no backup ever held a node configuration. Either way that step was unperformable under `STO-1`'s "A dead node never rejoins" before this bead.

Closed by `980ed3d` (`spec: the spend chapter's two Formal scope paragraphs name their theorems' premises, stopping points and fixtures, and say what no theorem carries (bps-axj.3)`). It sits on top of the claim `2143361`, and the base is `b1055f8`. Every check below was run on the landed tree after its last edit, with no other build running on it.

**Re-measured at the base**

`git diff e63715d b1055f8 --stat -- 04-spend-lifecycle.md tools/formal` printed nothing, so the bead's measurement still held.

The two paragraphs named 18 distinct `BtcPolicy.` names, all in the declaration list:

- Fourteen have a row in the requirement index:
  - seven `SPN-34` theorems and two `SPN-37` theorems;
  - `Kernel.register` and `Kernel.pairAdmits` (`SPN-32`);
  - `Kernel.born` (`DUR-11`);
  - `Kernel.shrinkTarget` (`DUR-14`);
  - `Silence.respond` (`API-12`).
- The other four are not tagged declarations:
  - `Kernel.Cand.acceptanceTimes` is a structure field;
  - `Kernel.Registration.preserve` and `Kernel.ExpiryRead.registered` are constructors of guard parameters;
  - `Silence.wfEvent` is an untagged `def`.

Five `SPN-34` theorems were named in neither paragraph, nor in any Markdown file:

- `Kernel.acceptanceTimes_origin` and `Kernel.withWindow_acceptanceTimes` are single-step lemmas behind `Kernel.resident_acceptanceTimes_preserved`.
- `Silence.AcceptanceTimesCases.acceptanceTimes_target_premises` shows that the `idAlone` exhibit's rules meet the five rule premises of `Silence.silence`.
- `Silence.acceptanceTimes_pub` and `Silence.pubCand_acceptanceTimes` are lemmas of the two-run silence proof.

None of them carries a clause beyond what the named theorems carry, and none is credited elsewhere. `Kernel.withWindow_acceptanceTimes` is now named, for the window write inside `Kernel.accept`. No theorem changed, so the index is unchanged.

**The claims (Work item 1) and what each now carries.** Names below drop the `BtcPolicy.` prefix; the text writes them in full.

After `SPN-34`:

- **"records the accepting step's effective first-seen instant and the born spend record's fire time together"** is what `Kernel.born` computes through `Kernel.register`. It is a definition; nothing was added.
- **"carries the spend commitment id"** is `Silence.respond`'s accept arm. It is a definition.
- **"reads those recorded instants for an accepted repeat while the pair is resident"** now carries three things:
  - the two exhibits, each with its fixture:
    - `Exhibits.TwoRun.accepted_repeat_keeps_instants`, under `Silence.current`, `Ledger.current` and `Kernel.current`, with `Exhibits.TwoRun.cfg`, `Exhibits.TwoRun.holdSys` with Hold 300 and `Exhibits.TwoRun.tblN` in both runs, on `Exhibits.TwoRun.acceptanceTimesTrace`;
    - `Silence.AcceptanceTimesCases.accepted_repeat_keeps_instants_under_idAlone`, under `Silence.Marker.committed` and its own spelled rules with the withdrawn `Kernel.EntryTarget.idAlone`, with its own guards, configuration, state, tables and trace;
  - `Kernel.resident_acceptanceTimes_preserved`, credited for one `Kernel.step`;
  - "no theorem carries the rest … over a composed `Ledger.sysStep` or a run".

  `Registration.preserve` cites `SPN-32`.
- **"the response does not depend on the incoming spend's fire time"** is carried by `Silence.respond_resident_ignores_fireAt`, for one `Silence.respond` answer, over all its binders. Its four hypotheses stand beside it: `Registration.preserve` (`SPN-32`), `ExpiryRead.registered` (`SPN-30`), and a resident under the spend's id that `pairAdmits` admits as this pair (`SPN-32`).
- **"incoming copies of the recorded value have no authority"** is carried by two theorems, with no hypotheses and all binders named:
  - `Kernel.accept_ignores_request_acceptanceTimes`, for one `Kernel.accept` node;
  - `Silence.respond_ignores_request_acceptanceTimes`, for one answer.

  Then: "No theorem carries the rest over a composed `Ledger.sysStep` or a run."
- **"preservation across a kernel step with duplicate-free resident ids under preserving registration"** is carried by `Kernel.resident_acceptanceTimes_preserved`, with all five hypotheses (`hn` before the step) and `SPN-32` cited. It takes no premise on reachability or the selected entry's target. `Kernel.ids_nodup` proves the duplicate-free premise on every `Kernel.Reachable` world under preserving registration (`SPN-32`).
- **"Once the pair has left the registry, registration records the new request's instants"** now carries four things:
  - `Exhibits.TwoRun.collected_pair_records_new_instants`, with its fixture, on `Exhibits.TwoRun.acceptanceTimesAfterPrune`;
  - `Kernel.shrinkTarget_registered`, for one `Kernel.register` lookup: with no candidate under the spend's id, `Kernel.shrinkTarget` and `Kernel.born` give the accepting effective sample and the incoming spend's fire time;
  - `Kernel.withWindow_acceptanceTimes`, for one window write inside `Kernel.accept`;
  - "No theorem carries the rest … over a run."
- **Reports, definitions and scope statements**, with nothing added:
  - the collection route's Carrier expiry;
  - "claims nothing about a node following the text there";
  - "The formal model has no replay log";
  - the repeat when a candidate is resident under the spend's id (`SPN-32` cited);
  - "carries no PSBT bytes or ladder";
  - "neither a rendered `remaining_secs` nor serialized response bytes";
  - "not runtime conformance".
- **"a request whose PSBT bytes changed is answered as such a repeat"**: "No theorem carries this."

After `SPN-37`:

- **"clears the fire time on the Escape member it births, keeps the spend's fire time as given, and leaves residents as they are"** is what `Kernel.register` computes. `Registration.preserve` cites `SPN-32`. It is a definition.
- **"an acceptance is independent of the incoming Escape record's fire time"** now carries three things:
  - `Kernel.accept_ignores_escape_fireAt`, for one `Kernel.accept` node, with no hypotheses and all binders named;
  - the exhibit `Exhibits.TwoRun.request_escape_fireAt_keeps_effects_and_registry`, with its fixture: `Ledger.current`, `Kernel.current`, `Exhibits.TwoRun.cfg`, `Exhibits.TwoRun.holdSys` with Hold 300, each of `tblN` and `tblD` with every request presenting a PIN ordinary under both, and `Exhibits.TwoRun.requestEscapeFireTrace` at the two Escape fire times over every prefix;
  - "No theorem carries the rest of … over a `Silence.respond` answer, a composed `Ledger.sysStep` or a run."
- **"That trace is the kernel's"**, "This checks registration's fire time; the request-shape boundary remains `Silence.wfEvent`" and "not runtime conformance" are scope statements.

The "show"/"proves" split holds clause by clause. The four fixture exhibits "show", and every theorem over quantified inputs "proves". No base word changed.

**Done when**

1. *Every claim carries its premises in its theorem's words and cites the theorem, or says no theorem carries it.*
   - The list above covers every claim.
   - Each premise was read against its declaration's hypotheses and binders, with none dropped and none added beyond the cited owners. The owners are `SPN-32` for preserving registration and for the pair `pairAdmits` admits, and `SPN-30` for gate 27's registered reading.
   - Each pointer states its stopping point: one `Silence.respond` answer, one `Kernel.accept` node, one `Kernel.step`, one `Kernel.register` lookup, or one window write. Each exhibit states its fixture.
   - Each no-theorem sentence was checked against every general declaration whose conclusion could state part of what it disclaims.
2. *Each gap found is its own bead.* One gap was found and filed: `bps-vpmi`.
   - **The gap:** `SPN-34`'s "fixed at first acceptance and replayed verbatim thereafter" against three texts:
     - its own residency bound;
     - `SPN-41`'s acceptance with a request's own `first_seen` and `remaining_secs` after the armed removal;
     - `SPN-23` and `SPN-24`'s retained keys.
   - **The bead:** a bug, P3, `needs-triage`, citing `bps-axj`, in `bps-xyu`'s form.
     - It quotes every side at `b1055f8`.
     - It cites `bps-rz5`'s closing comment, which listed the same question as left open with no bead.
     - It decides no direction.
   - **No gap in the other comparisons:**
     - the replay log against the collection route, which the paragraph's disclaimer absorbs;
     - `SPN-23` and `DUR-14`'s repeat reading of the resident's `fire_at`, against `Kernel.shrinkTarget`;
     - `SPN-30`'s gate 27 and `SPN-32`'s compatible pair, against `respond_resident_ignores_fireAt`'s premises;
     - `SPN-37`'s Escape with no fire window, against `Kernel.register` and `Silence.wfEvent`;
     - every named declaration's docstring.
3. *The gate is green unpiped.* The command was `flock … nix develop --command bash tools/check-all.sh`, unpiped and redirected to a file, in the repository on the landed tree. Exit 0, 94 s, all nine gates PASS (formal, identifiers, fixtures, obligations, coverage, citations, vectors, copies, regions), "All gates passed.".

**Scope, names and quotes**

- **Scope.**
  - `git diff b1055f8 --stat` lists `.beads/issues.jsonl` (the claim) and `04-spend-lifecycle.md` (75 insertions, 32 deletions, re-wrapping included).
  - Its three hunks all lie inside the two "Formal scope:" paragraphs, and every byte outside them is the base's.
  - `git diff --check b1055f8` prints nothing.
  - Nothing under `tools/`, `.github/`, `docs/` or `flake.*` changed.
- **Insert only.** A token-level check confirms the edit only inserts. Every base word, punctuation mark and backticked span of each paragraph is kept, in order: 268 tokens became 706, and 122 became 236.
- **Names.** The two paragraphs hold 73 backticked names, 45 of them distinct. Each was found at its declaration under `tools/formal/`, outside the build directory, and once in the declaration list.
- **Quotes.** The additions hold three quotes. Each quotes the paragraph's own base words, unattributed, so the citation gate checks none of them. Each occurs once in the base file under a whitespace-collapsed grep:
  - "reads those recorded instants for an accepted repeat while the pair is resident";
  - "Once the pair has left the registry, registration records the new request's instants";
  - "an acceptance is independent of the incoming Escape record's fire time".

  No quote attributed to a requirement, a Lean declaration or an ADR was added.
- **Citation gate.**
  - Locally it printed "quoted attributions verified: 894, 522 of them in Lean docstrings: clean" at the base and on the landed tree, and "unquoted attributions: 0: clean".
  - "BtcPolicy names resolved" went from 789 to 839, one per added name occurrence.
  - The local count includes the owner review documents, which CI does not read. On CI's corpus the names count went from 750 to 800.

**How it got here**

There were two rounds. Four independent reviewers (A to D) read each one, and every reviewer ran its gates in a clone of its own.

- **Round 1** annotated every clause and drafted the gap. One reviewer found that "No theorem carries the rest of" the residency clause disclaimed the step `resident_acceptanceTimes_preserved` carries.
- **Round 2** did four things:
  - credited that theorem;
  - re-tested every no-theorem sentence. The collection sentence had also disclaimed the one-registration part `shrinkTarget_registered` carries, and now credits it;
  - moved the `SPN-37` sentence after its exhibit and named its clause;
  - named `Silence.Marker.committed`.
- **Edits after review.** The Manager made three edits to the gap's text when filing it, and none to the specification:
  - dropped the sentence "Resolving that boundary needs an owner decision.", whose wording is the stop phrase and whose point **Done when** item 1 already makes;
  - changed "This draft" to "This bead";
  - removed one blank line.

No implementer or reviewer reported a refused or timed-out command, and every reviewer reported running its gates only in its own clone. The notes that ask for no change are in this bead's previous comment.
